WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.682
Welcome to Module 4 of the
Attribute-Driven Migration learning path:

2
00:00:04.682 --> 00:00:06.388
move Group Policy as code.

3
00:00:06.388 --> 00:00:11.338
This module serves three of the
implementation guide's gates, 0, 5 and 8,

4
00:00:11.338 --> 00:00:16.288
and takes Chapter 06 of the Federal
Modernization Workbook's Book 19.

5
00:00:16.288 --> 00:00:21.051
You'll read Group Policy analytics
into a move plan, one row per setting.

6
00:00:21.051 --> 00:00:24.679
You'll keep each settings catalog
policy as a reviewed file,

7
00:00:24.679 --> 00:00:27.938
with an owner and a decision
record for every setting.

8
00:00:27.938 --> 00:00:30.897
And you'll run a sync that
reads the tenant first,

9
00:00:30.897 --> 00:00:33.401
and creates only what its dry run showed.

10
00:00:33.401 --> 00:00:35.513
Then you'll run it all on your laptop,

11
00:00:35.513 --> 00:00:39.375
against a fake Graph and a fixture
tenant, and break it on purpose.

12
00:00:39.375 --> 00:00:44.830
The code is illustrative: tested against
fixtures, not against a production tenant.
